  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An Eastern Pacific upper-level area of\nlow pressure will move inland over Northern California this\nafternoon. High temperatures throughout Northern and Central\nNevada this afternoon will be two to four degrees below normal for\nthis time of year. The aforementioned cyclone aloft will progress\neastward across the forecast area this evening into Wednesday\nmorning, resulting in a chance of light precipitation. Snow \nlevels will start at around 7,000 feet this evening, before \ndropping to about 5,500 feet tonight. The majority of this light\nprecipitation will fall tonight. \n\nA ridge of high pressure will build northward across the Silver\nState Thursday through Monday. As a result, dry weather is\nexpected in Northern and Central Nevada. A warming trend is \nanticipated Thursday through Sunday. By Sunday afternoon, high \ntemperatures across Northern and Central Nevada will be six to\neight degrees above seasonal values. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding light precipitation in parts of Northern and Central \nNevada this evening through Wednesday morning. High forecast\nconfidence in a warming trend Thursday through Sunday. Moderate \nforecast confidence in dry weather Thursday through at least \nMonday. No deviations from the NBM model output.",
